From e3305f4c3b0a7c2ae9871b0e227cd4535880dd8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abel Melman <abel.melman@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:33:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(notifications): keep chat prompt and auto_send in the
 native macOS panel

The native panel re-encodes the clicked action from NotificationAction
before handing it to Rust (notification_panel.swift, onAction). The
struct had no prompt or auto_send, so a documented `chat` button
(screenpipe-api SKILL.md) lost its prompt on macOS, and auto_send: false
was dropped.

Adds both fields, plus a swiftc-only regression test:
bun run test:notification-panel-actions fails on 4162e6a34 with
"FAIL: prompt survives the click" and passes with this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
